/*
 * Wave Race 64: Recompiled - recompui stylesheet.
 *
 * MINIMAL, DELIBERATELY. Almost none of recompui's appearance comes from here:
 * the look is a C++ theme (recompui::theme) with ~90 named colours, border
 * radii and typography presets, all of which already have defaults. This file
 * only has to give the document its base text style, which RmlUi cannot infer.
 *
 * The font-family below MUST be the font's INTERNAL family name, which RmlUi
 * reads from the TTF's name table - not the filename, and not what the filename
 * looks like it implies. LatoLatin-Regular.ttf reports:
 *
 *     nameID 1 (Family)      = "LatoLatin"
 *     nameID 4 (Full name)   = "LatoLatin Regular"
 *     nameID 6 (PostScript)  = "LatoLatin-Regular"
 *
 * It is "LatoLatin". Getting this wrong does not warn and does not fall back:
 * RmlUi simply resolves no font face and every piece of text renders as
 * nothing at all, while the panels, sliders and layout draw perfectly.
 *
 * This is loaded at RUN time from assets/, so changing it costs a re-run and
 * not a rebuild.
 */

body {
    font-family: LatoLatin;
    font-weight: normal;
    font-style: normal;
    font-size: 20dp;
    color: #ffffff;
}
